version: 0.10.0
date-released: "2026-07-10"
url: "https://github.com/seap-udea/MontuPython"
repository-code: "https://github.com/seap-udea/MontuPython"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  MontuPython (mnṯw ꜥꜣpp(y)) is a Python package to compute astronomical
  ephemerides in the ancient world — thousands of years before the present.
  It was developed for ancient Egypt and applies equally to other sites of
  cultural and archaeoastronomical interest.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - archaeoastronomy
  - ancient Egypt
  - ephemerides
  - cultural astronomy
  - Python
identifiers:
